Backport from mainline Linux ("SPI" row of the CIX upstream wiki; the Sky1 SPI
controllers use the Cadence SPI driver, cix,sky1-spi-r1p6 / cdns,spi-r1p6).
The vendor driver keeps its own "fifo-width" (32-bit FIFO) support; these
mainline fixes are ported on top of it:

- 633cd6fe6e1 "spi: spi-cadence: Reverse the order of interleaved write and
  read operations": the interrupt handler refilled the TX FIFO before draining
  the RX FIFO, so on transfers longer than the FIFO received words were pushed
  out of a full RX FIFO and lost (corrupted reads from SPI flash, displays,
  ADCs, spidev on the 40-pin header).
- d9eadfce2fa "spi: spi-cadence: Move TX FIFO full busy-wait into FIFO": the
  TX-FIFO-full back-off was done once per transfer instead of per FIFO entry,
  so writes could be dropped while refilling and the transfer then timed out.
- 666fa7e9ca9 "spi: cadence: fix controller deregistration",
  5b1689a41f0 "spi: cadence: fix unclocked access on unbind",
  ecea4f0e9db "spi: cadence: fix clock imbalance on probe failure":
  unregister the controller before disabling it, resume it before touching its
  registers on unbind (an unclocked register access can hang the SoC), and keep
  runtime PM / clock counts balanced on probe failure (also fixes a vendor-only
  leak of the manually enabled ref_clk on probe failure and on unbind).

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-cadence.c b/drivers/spi/spi-cadence.c
index 39a0cf028..d15e581b0 100644
